/-
RVK fixed-base per-rung deployed-row certificate — GENERATOR TARGET TEMPLATE.

This file is the verified emission contract for the `leangen.rs` rvk fixed-base
rung-certificate generator (Workstream A, step 6). It is design-only (NOT imported
into `ShielddGnarkFormal.lean`); it pins, against the ACTUAL deployed rows of
note_reshape2x1 inst0, the exact shape every generated `rung_i` theorem must take.
Both theorems below were verified green and axiom-clean
(`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`).

Two cases are shown:
  • `rung1` — BASE case (rung 1): accumulator acc1 = bit0·G has NO carried
    select-delta wires.
  • `rung2` — INDUCTIVE case (rung 2): acc2 carries rung-1's select-delta wires
    d1x,d1y (in the full ladder these are the single rematerialized accumulator
    wires s_x,s_y), so the v2-product factors gain extra terms.

Per-rung emission contract (what the generator must produce for rung i):

1. Fact-FREE `decide` coefficient bindings. Every folded numeral coefficient in
   the deployed rows is rewritten to its symbolic product in Cᵢ-coords
   (= Lᵢ.x, Lᵢ.y, read directly off the addX row) and acc-form coords
   (Gx, Gy-1, a, d). Needed because `linear_combination`/`ring` over `ZMod Order`
   does NOT reduce numerals mod Order: a folded coeff and its integer product are
   equal mod p but not syntactically. After `simp only [bindings] at <rows>` both
   sides expand to identical integer polynomials and `ring` cancels — no mod-p
   reduction. Binding RHS forms (Cᵢ = Lᵢ, a = Order-1, d = 3021):
     v2 left  b0-coeff = d·Lᵢy·Gx ;  carried-x-coeff = d·Lᵢy
     v2 right b0-coeff = Lᵢx·(Gy-1)
     addX RHS b0-coeff = Lᵢy·Gx + Lᵢx·(Gy-1)
     addY RHS b0-coeff = a·Lᵢy·Gx - Lᵢx·(Gy-1) + ((Gy-1) - Gx·a)·(Lᵢx+Lᵢy)
     selX/selY b0-coeff = -Gx / -(Gy-1)   (deployed bakes p-Gx / 1-Gy)

2. Fact-section `rung_i` theorem taking the 5 deployed rows verbatim (l*r=o in the
   `sx*(1±v2)=…` normal form) + `hacc : onCurve accᵢ` (threaded from the ladder
   induction) + booleanity, discharging the keystone's 5 obligations via
   `refine fixedRung_fixedStepRel i …; · rw [C_eq_Lᵢ]; simp; linear_combination …`.

3. `a = -1` normalization (uniform, deterministic — replaces the old per-rung
   correction). The carried acc.x delta wires appear in hAddY's
   `(acc.y - acc.x·a)·(Cx+Cy)` term with coefficient `a`. Expanding `a` to its
   `Order-1` literal makes deployed `+coord` differ from goal `-a·coord` by a
   p-multiple. Instead, after `simp only […, EdwardsBridge.a]` unfolds `a` to the
   literal, `rw [a_eq_neg_one]` (a Fact-FREE `decide` lemma
   `(<Order-1 literal>:F) = -1`) rewrites it to `-1`, so deployed `+coord` matches
   goal `-(-1)·coord` EXACTLY — no correction term, no per-rung integer to compute.
   The addY binding `e_fb0` is correspondingly stated with `-1` for `a`. This is
   rung-independent: every rung emits the identical tactic shape.

The generated `rung_i` theorems feed `RvkFixedBaseLadder.fixedLadder` and compose
via `fixedLadder_final_semantic` to `scalarMulFromBits`.
-/
